1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Yazid ibn Walid ibn Abd al-Malik - Yazid III. Yazid was the son of a Persian princess who had been given as a concubine to Caliph al-Walid I.[1] His mother was Shah-i Afrid, a daughter of Peroz. Al-Tabari quotes a 
2 CONC couplet of Yazid's on his own ancestry:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT I am the son of Chosroes, my ancestor was Marwan, Caesar was my grandsire and my grandsire was Khagan.[3] Tabari further records descriptions of Yazid as being tall and handsome.
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yazid_III
