1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [https://books.google.com/books?id=lQjkJOUcVIwC&pg=PA35&lpg=PA35&dq=Zubeida+Khatun,+wife+of+Malik-Shah&source=bl&ots=5h6pZ2rimG&sig=reGhqSBaBsqKwuYCVdSrdzoi_6I&hl=en&sa=X&ei=vWwyVdW8EMnksAT_mIDwBQ&ved=0CDEQ6
2 CONC AEwAw#v=onepage&q=Alp%20Arslan&f=false '''Continuity and Change in Medieval Persia'''] by Ann K.S. Lambton:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mu'ayyid al-Mulk, after an abortive attempt by the amir Oner to organize a rebellion, joined in Muhammad b. Malik-Shah, who was contesting Berk-Yaruq’s supremacy, and became his wazir in 492/1098-9. In the fighting between Berk-Ya
2 CONC ruq’s supporters and Muhammad’s, Zubaida Khatun was taken prisoner and Mu’ayyid al-Mulk had her strangled in Ray. During the second campaign between Muhammad and Berk-Yaruq, he was captured near Hamadan in 494/1100 and Berk-Yaruq 
2 CONC executed him in revenge for his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT * from [https://books.google.com/books?id=lQjkJOUcVIwC&pg=PA388&lpg=PA388&dq=Sulaiman-Shah,+great+grandson+of+qavurt&source=bl&ots=5h7i0Zo9dG&sig=tyWDVSzDFprN0kjFQPWy_am2eL8&hl=en&sa=X&ei=d_RjVY-NApD_yQSbw4HYCQ&ved=0CC4Q6AEwAg#v=o
2 CONC nepage&q=Sulaiman-Shah%2C%20great%20grandson%20of%20qavurt&f=false '''the same source'''], Zubaida is mentioned as the daughter of Yaquti b. Chagri Bey.
