1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tahir was the grandson of Amr Laith. After Amr was imprisoned, Tahir succeeded him in Zarang. His brother Jacob also had an influential presence in his government. Tahir also faced a strong faction of Leith's sons 
2 CONC who claimed to rule Sistan, such as Ali, the brother of Yaqub and Amr, who had been ousted when Tahir came to power; But the supreme power in this emirate was in the hands of a Turkish slave named Sabk, who had ambitious tendencie
2 CONC s and the idea of ​​independence. However, at this time, the Saffarids added Kerman to their territory and invaded Persia in 901 AD.
