2 CONT
2 CONT 3.          ALEXIOS Megas Komnenos ([1335/37]-[before 1349]).  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "his sons, the lord Alexios and the lord Kalojannes, were sent…along with their mother" to Constantinople after the dea
2 CONC th of "the emperor lord Basil the Grand Komnenos" in 1340[105].  It is assumed that he died before his younger brother´s accession in 1349.  
