1 TITL Hazrat Khawaja Syed
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hazrat Khawaja Syed Muhammad bin Ahmad Ali al-Badaoni Al-Bukhari, better known as '''Nizamuddin Auliya Al-Bukhari''' (1238–1325) was a prominent Sufi saint of the Chishti order in the Indian subcontinent, known for
2 CONC  his influence in Delhi during the Delhi Sultanate period. He was the son of Hazrat Syed Abdullah and Bibi Zulekha. Born in Badaun, he later moved to Delhi, where he became a leading spiritual figure, known for his emphasis on dev
2 CONC otion, charity, and service to people regardless of social or religious background. He became a disciple of Baba Fariduddin Ganjshakar and continued his spiritual lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT He established a khanqah in Delhi that became a centre of spiritual learning and public service, attracting disciples and visitors from different regions. His teachings focused on love, humility, and detachment from political auth
2 CONC ority, despite living during a time of strong royal presence. His shrine in Delhi remains a major site of visitation, and his legacy continues through the Chishti order and its influence on South Asian spiritual and cultural life.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
